{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_23","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,260p' /home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed218530468/3/codegen_prompts/4.md\"","aggregated_output":"你要为一个新的 ARC-AGI 风格题目实现代码。代码文件必须包含 `main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray` 和 `generate_input() -> np.ndarray`。\n\n## 新题位置\n\n- 描述目录：`/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed218530468/3`\n- 题号：`4`\n- 目标代码路径：`/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed218530468/3/4.py`\n\n## 新题描述\n\n<new_puzzle index=\"4\">\n- `description`：每个彩色 L 形指向一个目标方格，目标方格内绘制该 L 形的微缩完整矩形补全。\n- `Input structure`：背景为 Black。网格中有若干大小相同的 Grey 空心正方形方格（边长为 5 像素，单像素边框，内部 3×3 为空）。每个方格的外部恰好有一个彩色 L 形物体（由 3 个同色像素组成直角形状），L 形的直角开口朝向某个方向（上、下、左、右之一），并且 L 形的一条臂指向（即最近的延长线经过）恰好一个 Grey 方格。\n- `Rule`：\n  - 对每个 L 形，确定其\"指向\"的方格：沿 L 形长臂方向延伸，找到最先遇到的 Grey 方格。\n  - L 形本身是一个 2×2 正方形缺了一个角的形状。确定缺失角的位置（左上/右上/左下/右下）。\n  - 在目标方格的 3×3 内部空间中，用该 L 形的颜色画出一个 2×2 实心小正方形，放置在 3×3 空间中与缺失角相对的那个角落。例如：L 形缺失右下角，则 2×2 方块画在 3×3 内部的左上角。\n  - L 形在原位置保留不动。Grey 方格边框保持不变。\n- `Key insight`：解题者需要两步非平凡推理：第一步是识别 L 形的臂方向以确定其指向哪个方格（方向解码层）；第二步是发现 L 形的缺角位置与方格内填充位置之间的\"相对\"映射关系（形状→位置的反转层）——缺角并非指示填充位置，而是指示填充位置的镜像对角。\n</new_puzzle>\n\n## 机制相似参考题\n\n下面参考题由本地相似度流程自动选择：先用 `annotations`/docstring/代码特征抽取机制标签，再按机制相似度、文本相似度和代码特征相似度重排，并用 MMR 做去重。优先学习这些题的对象识别方式、随机生成器约束、边界条件处理，不要照搬旧题规则。\n\n已选参考：train/34cfa167, eval/2c181942, train/3ad05f52, train/538b439f, train/6350f1f4, train/5b37cb25, eval/dbff022c, eval/0934a4d8\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"1\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"34cfa167\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3008\nmechanism=0.3797\nlexical=0.0130\ncode_feature=0.3333\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:connected_components, object:frame, object:rectangle, operation:reflect, output:same_size, relation:between, relation:direction\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/34cfa167.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/34cfa167.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nComplete a four-corner framed rectangle from one decorated anchor rectangle and its diagonal mate.\n\nInput structure:\n- The background is the dominant color.\n- Two same-color solid rectangular anchors of the same size sit on opposite\n  diagonal corners, with the first anchor above-left of the second.\n- The upper-left anchor has two one-cell-thick vertical control bars to its\n  right and two one-cell-thick horizontal control bars below it.\n\nRule:\n- Copy the anchor rectangle into the two missing corners of the implied\n  larger rectangle.\n- Repeat the right-side control bars horizontally between the left and right\n  anchors, using their spacing as the period, and draw the outer top and\n  bottom borders in the first right-control color.\n- Repeat the below-side control bars vertically between the top and bottom\n  anchors, using the same period, and draw the outer left and right borders\n  in the first below-control color.\n\nKey insight: The small control bars are the first two ticks of two periodic\nframe patterns; the diagonal anchor supplies the opposite corner and the\nmissing two anchor copies.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"symmetry/pattern\",\n  \"src\": \"two same-color solid rectangular anchors, with two right control bars and two below control bars beside the upper-left anchor\",\n  \"dst\": \"the missing two anchor corners and periodic frame segments between all four anchors\",\n  \"transform\": \"copy the anchor rectangle into the missing corners; repeat the right-control colors across the top and bottom anchor rows and outer borders, and repeat the below-control colors down the left and right side bars using the same spacing\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"2\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"2c181942\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.2922\nmechanism=0.3502\nlexical=0.0131\ncode_feature=0.4286\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:connected_components, code:rotation, object:frame, object:sprite, object:square, operation:reflect, relation:direction, relation:inside\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/2c181942.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/2c181942.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nAttach monochrome sprites to the matching sides of a central hollow square.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg = background. A hollow NxN square (hub) with bg corners/interior and four differently-colored edges (top, bottom, left, right).\n- 2-4 monochrome sprites scattered on the grid, each matching one hub edge color.\n\nRule:\n- For each hub edge color, find the matching sprite outside the hub.\n- Rotate the sprite (0/90/180/270°) so its contact edge has exactly N-2 contiguous cells aligned with the hub side, and the rotated sprite is mirror-symmetric along the contact-edge axis (UD for left/right, LR for top/bottom).\n- Translate it to adjoin that hub side. \n- Clear everything else to bg; output is hub + attached sprites only.\n\nKey insight: Each edge color uniquely pairs a sprite to a side; symmetry along the contact-edge axis disambiguates the correct rotation.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"move_to_match\",\n  \"src\": \"solid monochrome sprite s\",\n  \"dst\": \"attach to an edge of hollow polychrome sprite d with bg corners and 4 differently-colored side edges\",\n  \"match_cond\": \"s.head.color == d.edge.color and s.head.length == d.edge.length\",\n  \"transform\": \"rotate s to align matching edge with d.side\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"3\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"3ad05f52\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.2717\nmechanism=0.3201\nlexical=0.0130\ncode_feature=0.4286\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:bfs, code:connected_components, object:frame, object:rectangle, object:sprite, object:square, relation:between, relation:inside\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/3ad05f52.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/3ad05f52.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nPaint the maze corridor and framed rooms lying on shortest paths between the two colored endpoint components.\n\nInput structure\n- The grid has a dominant background, one wall color forming thin orthogonal frames, and one endpoint/fill color.\n- The endpoint/fill color forms exactly two 4-connected solid rectangular components; their larger side lengths define the framed room sizes.\n\nRule\n- Treat wall pixels as blocked and every other pixel as passable.\n- Find every passable pixel that lies on a shortest 4-connected path between the two endpoint components.\n- Also fill any framed square room of an endpoint-derived size that intersects that shortest-path mask.\n\nKey insight\n- Shortest paths identify the route through open connector corridors, while the wall-bordered square rooms need to be expanded from the route centerline to their full interior.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"move_along_path\",\n  \"src\": \"one of two same-color endpoint components\",\n  \"dst\": \"the other same-color endpoint component\",\n  \"path\": \"shortest 4-connected route through non-wall pixels\",\n  \"trajectory\": \"paint background pixels on the route with the endpoint color\",\n  \"transform\": \"fill any wall-framed square room of an endpoint-derived size that the route crosses\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"4\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"538b439f\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.2823\nmechanism=0.3232\nlexical=0.0129\ncode_feature=0.5000\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:bfs, code:connected_components, object:rectangle, object:sprite, operation:reflect, output:same_size, relation:between, relation:inside\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/538b439f.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/538b439f.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nReflect the solid rectangular source objects across the full separator line and color the gap with the separator color.\n\nInput structure:\n- A dominant background contains one full-width or full-height one-pixel\n  separator line in a non-background color.\n- One other foreground color forms solid rectangular objects, all strictly on the same side of that separator.\n- Remaining non-background pixels are scattered distractors.\n\nRule:\n- Keep the input grid shape and unchanged pixels outside each affected corridor.\n- Mirror each source object across the separator line.\n- For every source object, recolor the rectangular strip between the\n  original object and its reflection to the separator color, then paint the\n  reflected object in the source color.\n\nKey insight:\n- The full straight line is a mirror axis; the real objects are identified\n  structurally as the only solid rectangles confined to one side, while\n  scattered pixels are noise that may be overwritten inside the corridor.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"symmetry/pattern\",\n  \"src\": \"solid rectangular foreground objects all on one side of the full separator row/column\",\n  \"dst\": \"their mirror positions across the separator line\",\n  \"transform\": \"copy each source object by reflection; recolor the rectangular strip between each source object and its mirror to the separator color, overwriting background or distractor pixels inside that strip\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"5\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"6350f1f4\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.2791\nmechanism=0.2873\nlexical=0.0185\ncode_feature=0.6667\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:bfs, code:connected_components, code:rotation, object:sprite, object:square, operation:reflect\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/6350f1f4.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/6350f1f4.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nDecode a block-grid image by swapping each sprite-coded cell with a solid cell and each blank cell with the sprite.\n\nInput structure\nThe grid is partitioned by black separator rows and columns into equal-size\nsquare blocks. Each block is either a copy of one two-color sprite or a\nuniform blank block of the sprite's minority color; grey pixels are erased\ncells that act as wildcards.\n\nRule\nInfer the repeated sprite from fully visible mixed-color blocks. Replace a\nblock matching that sprite, ignoring grey erasures, with a solid block of\nthe sprite's majority color. Replace a uniform blank block with the sprite.\nSeparator rows and columns, including grey erasures on them, become black.\n\nKey insight\nThe small sprite is a block-level code for one macro-cell state, and the\nuniform minority-color block is the other state; the output renders the\nopposite code in each macro-cell while cleaning erased pixels.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"symmetry/pattern\",\n  \"src\": \"regular block grid separated by black lines; each block is either a two-color sprite or a uniform blank block, with grey pixels as erasures\",\n  \"dst\": \"same block grid with the two block states swapped\",\n  \"transform\": \"infer the sprite from fully visible mixed-color blocks; sprite-coded blocks become solid majority-color blocks, blank blocks become the sprite, and separator/erasure pixels become black\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"6\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"5b37cb25\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.2630\nmechanism=0.3324\nlexical=0.0134\ncode_feature=0.2857\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:connected_components, object:frame, object:rectangle, object:sprite, output:same_size, relation:direction, relation:inside\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/5b37cb25.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/5b37cb25.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nFill each plus-shaped background notch with the color of the frame side it opens toward.\n\nInput structure\n- A one-cell-thick rectangular frame has four solid-colored sides and neutral corner pixels.\n- The frame interior contains a dominant background color and one foreground object color.\n- Some object boundaries contain five-pixel plus-shaped background notches.\n\nRule\n- Find every background plus whose opposite side is supported by foreground object pixels and whose open side faces one frame side.\n- Recolor the five pixels of that plus with the color of the facing frame side.\n- Leave all other pixels unchanged.\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
